## Context

Oscar accepted and deferred issue #56, then explicitly offered to take option 1 as a PR.
Implement it on upstream v1.14.0: a persisted paused flag, not a second build verb. The
existing `stop` remains a one-shot cancellation; `pause` sets the durable hold and
`resume` clears it without starting work.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Branch starts from current upstream `main` and the intervening release is read.
- [x] Pause persists through both SQLite and legacy JSON stores, including when idle.
- [x] Build, refresh, update, and semantic search auto-build create no work while paused.
- [x] Existing queries remain usable, and resume clears the hold without starting work.
- [x] Full upstream test suite, typecheck, lint, build, and diff check pass.
- [x] A PR is opened against `oscardvs/zoteus`, then panel-reviewed on the PR page.
